/P 657 0 R
/E (Continuous process of increasing the value of credentials in the job market;)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 658 0 R
/E (Due to the universalization of education at the basic level \(especially primary education\), there is a process of shifting the value of educational credentials to higher levels \(secondary and higher education\);)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 659 0 R
/E (The process of increasing the value of educational credentials in the job market to overcome the barriers of social origins coexists with the tendency for a relative loss of the value of educational credentials in the process of social mobility.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 660 0 R
/E (The relative decrease in the chances of mobility via educational credentials can lead to a series of factors: a\) deepening and crystallization of inequalities based on the perception of educational credentials as merit in society; b\) reconfiguration of individuals' perception of the advantages of pursuing higher education, centralizing options for the imperial professions \(engineering, law, and medicine\).)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
